-- title:
--   Degree over ℚ̄(j) bounded by degree over k(j)
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number and $H$ a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and write $\Gamma_H(M)$ for [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained by pushing forward along the inclusion of $\Gamma_0(M)$ the preimage of $H$ under the homomorphism [`CohCarrier.gamma0Units`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L121) sending $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ to the unit of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ given by its lower-right entry. Let $\ell$ be a prime not dividing $M$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `LiesOverPrime ℓ`, i.e. $\ell$ lies in the nonunits of $A$, and let $k =$ `IsLocalRing.ResidueField A`. For a field $K$, [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) denotes the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ generated over $K$ by all quotients $\bar p_f/\bar p_g$ of coefficientwise reductions to $K$ of integral power series $p_f, p_g \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ that are $q$-expansions of modular forms $f,g$ of a common weight on $\Gamma$, with $\bar p_g \neq 0$; and [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) denotes the intermediate field of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the image of $F₀$ under coefficientwise extension of scalars. Given $x$ in `qExpFunctionFieldC k (GammaH M H)` whose underlying Laurent series is the $j$-series [`ModularCurve.jqModC k`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) $= q^{-1}\cdot\overline{E_4^3\,\eta^{-24}}$ over $k$, and $y$ in the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (GammaH M H)` whose underlying Laurent series is `jqModC` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the conclusion is the inequality of module ranks: the rank of the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base-changed field over the subfield $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(y)$ generated by $y$ is at most the rank of `qExpFunctionFieldC k (GammaH M H)` over its subfield $k(x)$.
--
--   This is the degree half of the good-reduction statement for the modular curve $X_H(M)$ at a prime $\ell \nmid M$: the degree of the mod-$\ell$ $q$-expansion function field over $k(j)$ is at least the generic degree over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(j)$, which is the form in which irreducibility of the special fibre enters. It is used in the construction of integral models and specialisations of places of these function fields, for instance in the prolongation-datum and reduction lemmas for $q$-expansions at level $\Gamma_1$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_finrank_gammaH_le_finrank_gammaH_residueField_of_not_dvd.lean

